message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Donghyun-lang (동현랭): a Korean esoteric programming language with a browser playground"
type: software
version: "1.54"
date-released: "2026-11-03"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23689480"
authors:
  - family-names: Kim
    given-names: Dong Hyun
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9883-0229"
    affiliation: "Inha University College of Medicine"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Raspberry-Kim/donghyun-lang"
url: "https://raspberry-kim.github.io/donghyun-lang/"
abstract: >-
  Donghyun-lang is an esoteric programming language written in Korean.
  The repository contains the JavaScript interpreter, a browser playground
  that runs without installation or a server, a Python interpreter, the
  language specification and 70 example programs. Donghyun-lang is also the
  only control language of eight educational browser laboratories by the
  same author: Donghyuncho (Drosophila brain circuits on the FlyWire
  connectome), Donghyunpa (C. elegans touch circuits), Donghyunvil (village
  outbreaks on a real contact network), Donghyunjeon (a single-player
  turn-based strategy game with land, sea and air units), Donghyuncop (a
  one-button cave-flight game), Donghyunten (a number-pair puzzle),
  Donghyunwar (a single-player medieval turn-based tactics game) and
  Donghyundoom (the shareware DOOM Episode 1 in the browser). In every
  laboratory the setup is written only in Donghyun-lang.
keywords:
  - esoteric programming language
  - Korean
  - interpreter
  - programming education
  - JavaScript
  - Python
